      en: "Hissar Fortress is located approximately 30 kilometers west of Dushanbe and is one of Tajikistan's most significant historical monuments. The current structure, best known for its imposing main gate (Darvaza) featuring two massive towers, dates primarily from the 16th to 19th centuries, though the site has been settled since antiquity. Hissar once served as the residence of the governor of the Emir of Bukhara and was a critical strategic and commercial hub along the Silk Road. Within the fortress walls and in its immediate vicinity are two notable madrasas (Kuhna and Naw), which testify to the city's role as a center of scholarship and religious education. Extensive restoration work was carried out in the 1980s and 2010s to reconstruct the original appearance of the mud-brick walls and monumental architecture. Today, the fortress is a popular destination for tourists and wedding parties and houses a museum showcasing artifacts from the region's diverse history.",
